<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97349" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωφάω</span></b> , poet. and 
			Ion.
		 Frequentat. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρέφω</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn constantly</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλάκατα ς</span>. <i>keep
			turning</i> the wool, i.e. spin, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.53
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδάλιον παλάμῃ</span>”
				<i>steer,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					9.242
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλὴν ἀμφὶ πολὺν στρώφα χρόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.424
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμων . . βίου στρωφῶσα πορείην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					48.381
				</span></i>
			: —
				Pass.
			, <i>turn oneself about, keep turning</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ αὐτοὺς στρωφᾶτ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.557
				</span></i>
			; <i>roam about, wander</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηρὸν
				ἑκὰς ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				20.422
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δῆμόν τε πόλιν τε</span>
			<i>visit</i> cities, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				528
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽ Ἑλλάδα . ., ἀνὰ νήσους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					247
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὰ τὴν πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.85
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλῃ κἄλλῃ δωμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					907
				</span></i>
			: hence, <i>move freely in</i> a place, <i>abide</i>
			there, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ μέγαρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.463
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				60
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν λέχει στρωφώμενος</span>,
			i.e. claiming a husband's rights, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1224
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν νέοις στρωφωμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1052
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Διδύμοις στρωφωμένου ἠελίοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					285.16
				</span></i>
			; of the heavenly bodies, <i>revolve</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Man.
				2.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωφᾶν</span> for 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωφᾶσθαι, ἐπὶ γαῖαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.893
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				285.46
			</span></i>.</div>
